        "title": "Apple explains how to turn off the new MacBook Pro’s glowing logo",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/05/apple-explains-how-to-turn-off-the-new-macbook-pros-glowing-logo/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/11/macbook-pro-proled-xdr-touch-07.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While the illuminated Apple logo on the <a href=\"https://link.amazon/A0bspCQfK\">new MacBook Pro</a> drew one of the biggest cheers during last week’s announcement, Apple knows that not everyone will want to keep it on. Here’s the company’s official guide to turning it off.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"macbook-pro\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1077701\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/11/05/apple-explains-how-to-turn-off-the-new-macbook-pros-glowing-logo/#more-1077701\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
